The vector $\underset{\sim}{v}=6\underset{\sim}{i}-6\underset{\sim}{j}$ is drawn with $\underset{\sim}{i}$ pointing east and $\underset{\sim}{j}$ pointing north, as shown. Find the direction of $\underset{\sim}{v}$ as a true bearing.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[->] (-0.6,0)--(3.0,0) node[right]{$E$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.8)--(0,2.4) node[above]{$N$};
\draw[-{Stealth},thick] (0,0)--(2.2,-2.2) node[below right]{$\underset{\sim}{v}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
